    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0373" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg279"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note, No. 518, of
                    the 13th of October last, to Viscount Gough, and to previous correspondence in
                    regard to the arrangements for preventing the use of firearms in Bering Sea by
                    pelagic sealers, I have the honor to inform you that I am instructed by the
                    Marquis of Salisbury to state that Her Majesty’s Government agree to postpone
                    further discussion on this subject for the present.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
